      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Stratos: Zephyr's Flight [zone=1208]\n**Who:**\n- Dusky Iron Meditation [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Clear Heart of Unfettered Stone [item=134771]\n- Gemstone Heart of Unfettered Stone [item=134770]\n- Pile of Rubble [item=134280]\n- Writ of Entry - Esianti [item=134757]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Brass Palace [quest=9445]\n- Fight Fire [quest=9263]\n- Palace of Embers [quest=9433]\n- Partisan of Stratos: Zephyr's Flight (10 Points) [quest=9234]\n- Prisoner's Dilemma [quest=9265]\n- Soldier of Air [quest=9225]\n- Trial of Three (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9281]\n- Trial of the Ashes of Rusted Cliff's Glory (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9335]\n- Trial of the Eternal Cyclone (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9336]\n- Trial of the Speaker's Amphitheater (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9282]\n- Trial of the Wending Ways (Trial of Smoke) [quest=9337]\n**Era:** | !The Burning Lands\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Mon Nov 5 03:07:46 2018\nModified: Sun Mar 1 00:43:50 2026 | | **Prerequisite Quests: Soldier of Air [quest=9225], Fight Fire [quest=9263], and any one of Trial of Smoke, Prisoner's Dilemma [quest=9265], Palace of Embers [quest=9433], and Brass Palace. [quest=9445].**\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this quest from Dusky Iron Meditation in Stratos at -360, -646, +241 on the far southeast island.\nP 646.9178, 360.5342, 238.1304, 0, 0, 240, 2, Dusky\\_Iron\\_Meditation(Q)\nYou say, 'Hail, Dusky Iron Meditation'\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Ah, a mortal. Stratos seems infected with them now.'\nSay 'key to Esianti' to get him to talk to you and go through the text - or just say \"accept\".\nSay accept to get the task from Dusky Iron Meditation.\nIf you see in yellow txt \"Perhaps you should speak with Grieving Soul Scent in Stratos.\".\nThis means you need to do the Fight Fire shared task that you get from Grieving Soul Scent.\nYou will also need to do at least one of the Trials in Plane of Smoke.\nOther tasks also need to be completed, check the pre requisite tasks up above.\nYou say, 'key to Esianti'\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Oh, I am sorry. I did not intend to be rude, even to a mere mortal. I am distracted by the loss of my servant and will be so until it [returns]. I have such a key, but I will need it to complete my task.'\nYou say, 'returns'\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'I sent it on an errand of some great import and it has not yet returned. I cannot [seek it out], for should I do so it will certainly return here and be confused by my absence. I am sure you, as a mortal, understand. So I must await here.'\nYou say, 'seek it out'\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Ah, perhaps you have a point. Send a pebble to find a pebble, as they say. I could ask you to seek it out, but I am concerned that there will be issues entering a contract with a mortal. It would certainly be pointed out that you cannot understand the details of such a contract. Such a thing would contain greater risk for me than for you. However, my need is great. I have been sent on an errand that I must complete. It should have been simple and has become, as it always seems to, disturbingly [difficult].'\nYou say, 'difficult'\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Of course, this would be even more difficult for you. You mentioned that you were interested in a way to enter Esianti. I am willing to offer you access if, by some miracle, could assist me in accomplishing my [task].'\nYou say, 'task'\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Clever of you to ask. I seek payment for a delivery made to Stratos. The contract has been broken by the receiver and payment has not been made for the earth we delivered recently. I must recover that payment so that I may return to Mearatas. If you will [accept] a contract to assist me as needed to recover that payment, I will give you my Esianti key upon completion.'\nYou say, 'accept'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Key to the Kingdom'.\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'So be it. First you will need to discover where my servant has gone.'\n\n---\n\n**Version #1**\n06. Find Dusky Iron Meditation's servant. Unfettered Stone 0/1 Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\n\n\n> **Task Window:** Grieving Soul Scent has suggested you might be able to gain access to Esianti to find answers to how this war with the efreeti was started. Despite being told that is is none of his business, he still considers stopping the war to be extremely important. He feels that a continued battle will eat away a both realms.\n\n\n\nThis is a ground spawn, found in Stratos. It looks like a Brown dung rock called ( Pile of Rubble this can be Pre-looted) You can find it at /way 131, -335, 188 and on some of the other islands as well.\n\n07. Return the remains of Unfettered Stone to Dusky Iron Meditation 0/1 Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\n\n\n> **Task Window:** Return the recovered gemstone to Dusky Iron Meditation.\n\n\n\nThis step might have different versions depending on what ground spawn you loot.\n\n\n\n\nReturn to and Turn in the Pile of Rubble to Dusky Iron Meditation\n\n08. Find out how Unfettered Stone died 0/1 Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\n\n\n> **Task Window:** Discover how the geonid died from the evidence found on the rubble of Unfettered Stone and any witnesses you can find.\n\n\n\n\n\nHave people take turns talking to 3 NPC's. an upset dervish, a hidden mephit or a languishing courier.\n\n\nEach person in the group will need to talk to 1 of the 3 NPC's. Talking to the NPC's will spawn a specific mob (see below) to kill to get the Gem stone.\n\n\n\n\nan upset dervish spawns at /way 94, -301, 189. After going through the dialogue, it spawns a furtive elemental, kill it and loot Gemstone Heart of Unfettered Stone.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, an upset dervish'\n\n\n\n\nAn upset dervish says, 'Hello, strange creature. Why do you disturb me so? I have much to [think about] right at this moment.'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'think about'\n\n\n\n\nAn upset dervish says, 'I did something wrong. I did a thing for one of the earth, took it up to the tower. It wanted to see around before returning to its master. But then it [fell].'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'fell'\n\n\n\n\nAn upset dervish says, 'It fell. I guess it was not part of the air, and so would not be supported by it? Or that it was part of the earth and was drawn to it, very quickly drawn to it. It was turned into smaller versions of itself, but none of those could speak. And it stayed in one place until the [water being] came, and then until you came and took what the water left.'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'water being'\n\n\n\n\nAn upset dervish says, 'It came upon the small pieces of earth and took away from it some smaller piece of earth. It appeared as though it was doing as it should not, seemed worried that I would try to prevent it from taking the piece. Where it went I do not know. Please understand, I did not know that the earth would destroy one of its own like that.'\n\n\n\n\nIf an upset dervish tells you to go away, then you need to talk to either a hidden mephit or a languishing courier.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIf you talk to a hidden mephit at /way 260, 670, 209, it spawns a furtive dwarf you need to kill. It spawns at /way 283, 371, 188. Kill it and loot Gemstone Heart of Unfettered Stone.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, a hidden mephit'\n\n\n\n\nA hidden mephit says, 'Oh! A mortal! Please, do not destroy me like you did the [other]!'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'other'\n\n\n\n\nA hidden mephit says, 'Yes! You killed that poor earth creature! Don't try to convince me that you [did not] do so.'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'did not'\n\n\n\n\nA hidden mephit seems to calm down somewhat. 'Oh, well, you don't look so much like that one. It was very small, with... I believe you call it hair, all over its face. It came here and killed the earth being and skulked away! I don't want to think of it. And you make me nervous. Please leave.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nYou can find a languishing courier at /way 141, 743, 240. After the dialogue, it spawns a confused mud elemental at /way 431, 251, 199 on the bridge. Kill it and loot Gemstone Heart of Unfettered Stone.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, a languishing courier'\n\n\n\n\nA languishing courier says, 'Now is not the time to disturb me, I am resting, recovering from what I have been forced to [witness].'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'witness'\n\n\n\n\nA languishing courier says, 'It was a terrible thing, a thing that makes me churn to think of. A bumbling earth creature, moving far too fast and not looking where it was going, collided with an innocent tide, destroying both. The violence of it! Horrible. They were both destroyed and their destruction caused some misshapen monstrosity of mud to come into being. I... I cannot talk of it more.'\n\n09. Return the gemstone heart of Unfettered Stone to Dusky Iron Meditation. 0/1\n\n\n\n\n\n> **Task Window:** Return the recovered gemstone to Dusky Iron Meditation.\n\n\n\nReturn to and Turn in the Gemstone to Dusky Iron Meditation\n\n\n\n\nYou offered 1 Gemstone Heart of Unfettered Stone to Dusky Iron Meditation.\n\n\n\n\nYou have been given: Clear Heart of Unfettered Stone\n\n\n\n\nYour task 'Key to the Kingdom' has been updated.\n\n\n\n\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Well, this helps greatly! In the memory of Unfettered Stone is the information I need.' Dusky Iron Meditation cups the stone heart in both hands. Magic swirls through his fingers. When he holds the stone out to you it is changed, turned clear and glows slightly. 'Now, take this to an Udex. They will understand the contract involved, you will not, so do not try.'\n\n\n\n\nYou complete the trade with Dusky Iron Meditation.\n\n\n\n\nYou receive Clear Heart of Unfettered Stone.\n\n10. Bring Dusky Iron Meditation's evidence to an Udex and convince them to hear his case. 0/1 Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\n\n\n> **Task Window:** No text for this step\n\n\n\n\n\nHead over to and Turn in the Clear Gemstone to the Udex. This is the mob up the long stairs long name.\n\n\n\n\nThe Udex this step is talking about is at /way 12, 947, 280\n\n\nDifferent Udex named can spawn there.\n\n\n\n\nYou offered 1 Clear Heart of Unfettered Stone to Udex Ivory Wind Tyrant.\n\n\nThey give the stone back.\n\n\nYou have been given: Clear Heart of Unfettered Stone\n\n\nYour task 'Key to the Kingdom' has been updated.\n\n\nUdex Ivory Wind Tyrant peers into the stone and looks intent. After a moment the Udex says, 'You are the agent of this Dusky Iron Meditation, I see it in the contract. Tell your master that I grant his right to payment and authorize a mandate to enforce it. This contract shall serve as warrant.'\n\n\nYou complete the trade with Udex Ivory Wind Tyrant.\n\n11. Give the warrant stone to Dusky Iron Meditation so that the contract can be completed. 0/1 Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\n\n\n> **Task Window:** ?\n\n\n\nReturn to and Turn in the Warrant to Dusky Iron Meditation.\n\n\n\n\nYou offered 1 Clear Heart of Unfettered Stone to Dusky Iron Meditation.\n\n\nYour task 'Key to the Kingdom' has been updated.\n\n\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Ah, well done, I must say. This contract will serve my needs. Come forth and honor your debt!'\n\n\nYou complete the trade with Dusky Iron Meditation.\n\n\nAn empowered agent says, 'I come. My master acknowledges your right to payment. The full volume of air will be delivered directly to your master in Mearatas shortly.'\n\n\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Well, that will help. It is shocking how much air mortals consume. The requirement that we provide livable space for mortals seems like such a waste, but it must be done. How do you waste so much air? Never mind, it is done.'\n\n12. Speak with Dusky Iron Meditation. 0/1 Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Dusky Iron Meditation'\n\n\nYou have been given: Writ of Entry - Esianti\n\n\nYour task 'Key to the Kingdom' has been updated.\n\n\nDusky Iron Meditation says, 'Yes, yes, you have done your task well enough.'\n\n13. Tell Great Sky Ocean that you have the key to enter Esianti. 0/1 Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Great Sky Ocean'\n\n\nYour task 'Key to the Kingdom' has been updated.\n\n\nGreat Sky Ocean says, 'Well done! With that key you can seek the contract that Moon Serf of Harmonious Heavens must have signed. I can send you there, now that you have the right to enter, when you are ready to take on the [mission] set before you.'\n\n\nYou say, 'mission'\n\n\nGreat Sky Ocean says, 'Good! I am glad you are still willing. I will send you to Esianti whenever you are ready [to go].'\n\n\nYou have been assigned the task 'Contract of War'.\n\n\nYou have gained 10 ability point(s)!\n\n\nYou have completed achievement: Vindicator of The Burning Lands (Group)\n\n\nYou have completed achievement: Partisan of Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\nYou have successfully been granted your reward for: Vindicator of The Burning Lands (Group)\n\n\nYou say, 'to go'\n\n\n---\n\n**Version #2 (Let me know if these are the right steps for this version.)**\n06. Find Dusky Iron Meditation's servant. Unfettered Stone 0/1 Stratos: Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\n\n\n> **Task Window:** Grieving Soul Scent has suggested you might be able to gain access to Esianti to find answers to how this war with the efreeti was started. Despite being told that is is none of his business, he still considers stopping the war to be extremely important. He feels that a continued battle will eat away a both realms.\n\n\n\nThis is a ground spawn, found in Stratos. It looks like a Brown dung rock called ( Pile of Rubble this can be Pre-looted)\n\n07. Return the remains of Unfettered Stone to Dusky Iron Meditation 0/1 Straot;s Zephyr's Flight\n\n\n\n\n\n> **